# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values -- .env itself is
# gitignored so secrets never get committed.
#
# agent-review / agent-init load .env automatically (via python-dotenv),
# searching upward from whatever directory you run the command FROM --
# not from wherever the CLI package itself is installed, and not
# downward into subdirectories. Concretely:
#
#   - Put .env in the directory you `cd` into before running
#     agent-review/agent-init (or any parent of it). If you followed this
#     project's own README and normally run these commands from this
#     repo's root (e.g. `cd code-review-agents; .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1;
#     agent-review --path ...`), put .env at THIS repo's root --
#     NOT inside cli/, even though this template file lives there. A
#     .env in cli/ is invisible to a command run from the repo root,
#     since the search only ever looks upward, never down into
#     subdirectories.
#   - A real `$env:FOO=...` / `export FOO=...` you've already set always
#     wins over whatever .env has for the same name.
#   - If python-dotenv somehow isn't installed, this is silently skipped
#     -- exporting the variables yourself still works exactly as before.
#
# See cli/README.md's Install section for the full explanation of every
# variable below, including the $env:FOO = "..." / export FOO=...
# equivalents for setting these directly instead of via .env.

# Required: your Microsoft Foundry (Azure AI Foundry) resource name --
# the "example-resource" in https://example-resource.services.ai.azure.com/anthropic/.
# This is the exact env var name the `anthropic` SDK's AnthropicFoundry
# client reads on its own; don't rename it. See naming rules (2-64 chars,
# lowercase letters/numbers/hyphens, must start and end alphanumeric, and
# must be globally unique across Azure since it's a public subdomain) in
# cli/README.md.
ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_RESOURCE=your-foundry-resource-name

# Auth option 1 (default): a static API key for the above resource.
# Leave unset if you're using Entra ID auth (option 2) instead.
ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_API_KEY=

# Auth option 2: Entra ID (Azure AD) instead of a static key. Set to 1 to
# enable; requires the optional azure-identity dependency
# (pip install azure-identity, or pip install -e ".[azure-ad]") and
# whichever account `DefaultAzureCredential` resolves (Azure CLI login,
# managed identity, etc.) must have access to the Foundry resource above.
# Leave unset/0/false/no/off if you're using an API key instead -- do not
# set both auth options.
ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_USE_ENTRA_ID=

# Optional, advanced: overrides the resource-derived URL entirely with a
# custom base URL. Mutually exclusive with ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_RESOURCE --
# leave this unset unless you have a specific reason to override the
# standard https://<resource>.services.ai.azure.com/anthropic/ endpoint
# (e.g. a private endpoint / custom DNS setup).
# ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_BASE_URL=

# Not an env var -- the model is chosen with --model on the command line
# (default: claude-sonnet-5, see cli/src/agent_review/agents_client.py).
# e.g. agent-review --path <repo> --model claude-opus-5
